Meta:
@profile web/desktop/chrome

Scenario: 1. Verify the page title
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//header)` appears
Then `${current-page-url}` matches `https://www.epam.com/?`

Scenario: 2. Verify the ability to switch between Light and Dark modes
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//header)` appears
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//div[contains(@class, 'theme-switcher')] | //button[contains(@class, 'theme-switcher')])` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//div[contains(@class, 'theme-switcher')] | //button[contains(@class, 'theme-switcher')])`
Then number of elements found by `xpath(//header)` is EQUAL_TO `1`

Scenario: 3. Verify the ability to change the site language to Ukrainian
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//header)` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//button[contains(@class, 'location-selector') or contains(text(), 'Global')])`
When I click on element located by `xpath(//a[contains(@href, 'epam.ua') or contains(text(), 'UA')])`
Then `${current-page-url}` matches `https://.*epam\.ua.*`

Scenario: 4. Verify the policies list
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//footer)` appears
Then number of elements found by `xpath(//footer//a)` is EQUAL_TO `22`

Scenario: 5. Verify the ability to switch location lists by region
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//footer)` appears
Then number of elements found by `xpath(//footer)` is EQUAL_TO `1`

Scenario: 6. Verify the search function
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//button[contains(@class, 'header-search__button')])` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//button[contains(@class, 'header-search__button')])`
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//input[contains(@placeholder, 'What are you looking for') or @type='text'])` appears
When I enter `AI` in field located by `xpath(//input[contains(@placeholder, 'What are you looking for') or @type='text'])`
When I click on element located by `xpath(//button[contains(text(), 'FIND') or contains(@class, 'custom-search-button')])`
Then number of elements found by `xpath(//div[contains(@class, 'search-results') or contains(@class, 'search-result')])` is GREATER_THAN `0`

Scenario: 7. Verify form field validation
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//a[contains(@class, 'cta-button-ui') or .//span[text()='CONTACT US']])` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//a[contains(@class, 'cta-button-ui') or .//span[text()='CONTACT US']])`
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//button[contains(@class, 'submit') or contains(text(), 'SUBsubmit') or @type='submit'])` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//button[contains(@class, 'submit') or contains(text(), 'SUBMIT') or @type='submit'])`
Then number of elements found by `xpath(//span[contains(@class, 'error') or contains(@class, 'validation') or contains(@class, 'required')])` is GREATER_THAN `0`

Scenario: 8. Verify that the company logo in the header leads to the main page
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//header)` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//a[contains(@class, 'header__logo')])`
Then `${current-page-url}` matches `https://www.epam.com/?`

Scenario: 9. Verify the ability to download a report
Given I am on main application page
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//a[@href='/about' and contains(text(), 'About')])` appears
When I click on element located by `xpath(//a[@href='/about' and contains(text(), 'About')])`
When I wait until element located by `xpath(//a[contains(text(), 'Corporate Overview') or contains(@href, 'Corporate-Overview')])` appears
When I scroll element located by `xpath(//a[contains(text(), 'Corporate Overview') or contains(@href, 'Corporate-Overview')])` into view
When I click on element located by `xpath(//a[contains(text(), 'Corporate Overview') or contains(@href, 'Corporate-Overview')])`
Then file with name matching `.*Corporate-Overview.*` is downloaded
